THOUGHT: I need to confirm the current NullAway errors count and then adjust the code so that the enhanced-for loop iterates over a definitely non-null array. The simplest fix is to introduce a local non-null variable inside the includeRemoteRegion block, assigned from remoteRegions, and iterate over that. This leverages the existing null check used to compute includeRemoteRegion and should not change behavior. After editing, I’ll re-run the build to ensure the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/eureka && sed -i '812,816s/if (includeRemoteRegion) {/if (includeRemoteRegion) {
      String[] nonNullRemoteRegions = remoteRegions;
      if (nonNullRemoteRegions == null) {
        throw new IllegalStateException("remoteRegions is null despite includeRemoteRegion being true");
      }/;812,816s/for (String remoteRegion : remoteRegions)/for (String remoteRegion : nonNullRemoteRegions)/' eureka-core/src/main/java/com/netflix/eureka/registry/AbstractInstanceRegistry.java && ./gradlew eureka-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -i "NullAway" new_build_output.log | tail -n 5 || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log```

